# Frontend (Next.js App Router)

## Confirm routing model

- This repository uses the **App Router** under `src/app/` only. There is **no** `pages/` router tree—do not add `src/pages` or Pages Router APIs (`getServerSideProps`, `getStaticProps`, `pages/api`).
- New routes belong as `src/app/<segment>/page.tsx` (and related `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx` only when consistent with neighboring routes).

## Ground truth before edits

- Open the files you will change and **one level of callers/layouts** so imports, metadata, and `'use client'` boundaries match existing patterns.
- Do **not** invent components, hooks, or imports—reuse `@/components/design/*`, `@/lib/site`, `@/lib/motion`, etc., or add only what the user explicitly requested.

## Server vs client

- Default to **Server Components**. Add `'use client'` only where the file already uses interactivity or the change requires hooks/browser APIs; keep client boundaries **small** (see root `.cursorrules`).

## Dynamic routes and runtime APIs

- If you add or edit dynamic segments, follow **current Next.js** async conventions for `params` / `searchParams` and for `cookies()` / `headers()` as used elsewhere in the repo.
- Do not assume experimental flags or config keys that are not present in `next.config.ts`.

## Editing style

- **Incremental** diffs; preserve formatting, naming, and file structure.
- **Do not delete** unrelated code or comments.
- Maintain **strict TypeScript**—verify types after edits; never widen to `any` to silence errors.

## Overlap with root rules

- Stack, SEO, analytics, and Motion specifics live in **`.cursorrules`**—follow that file; this rule file adds **routing verification** and **no-invention** discipline for frontend paths.
